      <p class="parallel-check-instructions">
        This is the same parallel pair from "Check your understanding," now solved algebraically. Total
        current I leaves the battery, splits into I<sub>1</sub> and I<sub>2</sub> across the two
        resistors, then recombines into I again before returning — trace the derivation alongside it to
        see why that split forces the combined resistance down.
      </p>
      <div class="split-columns">
        <div class="split-diagram">
          <div class="parallel-check-board derivation-board" data-testid="derivation-board">
            <svg
              class="parallel-check-circuit"
              viewBox={`0 0 ${CHECK_VIEWBOX.width} ${CHECK_VIEWBOX.height}`}
              role="img"
              aria-label="A closed parallel circuit: total current I splits into I1 and I2 across two resistors, then recombines into I"
            >
              <defs>
                <marker
                  id="derivation-arrow"
                  viewBox="0 0 10 10"
                  refX="8"
                  refY="5"
                  markerWidth="6"
                  markerHeight="6"
                  orient="auto-start-reverse"
                >
                  <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z" fill="#f59e0b" />
                </marker>
