            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="derivation-steps" data-testid="derivation-steps">
          <ol>
            <li>
              Both resistors sit across the same two points, so they share one voltage: V = I·R<sub
                >total</sub
              > = I<sub>1</sub>·R1 = I<sub>2</sub>·R2.
            </li>
            <li>Ohm's law gives the current through each branch: I<sub>1</sub> = V/R1, I<sub>2</sub> = V/R2.</li>
            <li class="derivation-step-highlight" data-testid="derivation-step-kirchhoff">
              Kirchhoff's current law: the current splits and recombines, so <strong>I = I<sub
                >1</sub
